{"name":"Wild Geranium","hex":"#986a79","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"wild geranium","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A flowering plant of species Geranium maculatum, found in North America from Manitoba and Quebec to Oklahoma and Georgia."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wild_geranium"}],"entries":[{"title":"Geranium maculatum","blocks":[{"text":"Geranium maculatum, the wild geranium, spotted geranium, or wood geranium, is a perennial plant native to woodlands in eastern North America, from southern Manitoba and southwestern Quebec south to Alabama and Georgia and west to Oklahoma and South Dakota."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/Geranium_maculatum_Leatherwood_Lake.jpg/330px-Geranium_maculatum_Leatherwood_Lake.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Geranium_maculatum"},{"title":"Geranium","blocks":[{"text":"Geranium is a genus of 422 species of annual, biennial, and perennial plants that are commonly known as geraniums, hardy geraniums, or cranesbills. They are found throughout the temperate regions of the world and the mountains of the tropics, with the greatest diversity in the eastern part of the Mediterranean region."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Geranium_February_2008-1.jpg/330px-Geranium_February_2008-1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Geranium"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/G.maculatum.jpg/500px-G.maculatum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/G.maculatum.jpg/500px-G.maculatum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Flowers in late spring","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AG.mac